From 02e61375156230c5f361ad86d4c31216584d1eba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:36:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/38] compiler/zos: C records by value and as results like
 clang (XPLINK-64)

cdecl functions now pass and return records the way clang does for
z/OS, so that Pascal and C code can call each other with records of
any size:

- records of up to 24 bytes are returned in GPR 1-3 (inreg), also sizes
  that are not a multiple of 8 (left-justified in the last register);
  larger records via a hidden result pointer
- complex-like records (two float or two double fields) are passed and
  returned in FPRs (results in FPR 0 and 2)
- records passed by value always occupy full 64 bit slots; small records
  (1, 2, 4 bytes) are no longer passed as integers of their own size,
  and the last, partially filled slot of a larger record is no longer
  truncated and zero extended: the data is left-justified

Generic code: llvmgetcgparadef keeps the last location a full 64 bit
slot on s390x; gen_load_loc_cgpara no longer treats a record in several
FPU locations as a single floating point value; the LLVM code generator
loads and stores FPU locations of such records.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
